<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: TENNIS-INDIA WIN DOUBLES, LEAD CZECHS 2-1 IN DAVIS CUP TIE.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-INDIA WIN DOUBLES, LEAD CZECHS 2-1 IN DAVIS CUP TIE.</headline>
<dateline>PRIBRAM, Czech Republic 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>India took a 2-1 lead over the Czech Republic in their Davis Cup World Group first round tie, winning the doubles match on Saturday.</p>
<p>Result:</p>
<p>Leander Paes/Mahesh Bhupathi beat Petr Korda/Martin Damm 7-6 (9-7) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>India lead Czech Republic 2-1.</p>
</text>
